    {
      "id": "09280a27-d255-4dea-8eae-e8cd0b229a6e",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        976,
        -320
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 864,
        "content": "## Automated URL Phishing & Threat Analysis\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow accepts a submitted URL, normalizes it into a URL/domain record, then checks multiple threat intelligence and domain reputation sources. It enriches the URL with Safe Browsing, IP geolocation, RDAP domain age, certificate history, and VirusTotal analysis data before scoring the risk. An LLM produces a structured threat assessment, which is formatted, logged to Google Sheets, and sent to Slack as an alert.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure the form trigger fields so users can submit the URL in the expected input field.\n- Add API credentials or keys for Google Safe Browsing, VirusTotal, and Google Gemini.\n- Configure Google Sheets credentials and select the destination spreadsheet/sheet for logging reports.\n- Configure Slack credentials and choose the target workspace/channel for alerts.\n- Verify the HTTP request URLs and expressions reference the normalized URL and domain fields correctly.\n\n### Customization\n\nAdjust the JavaScript risk scoring logic, LLM prompt/output schema, wait duration for VirusTotal analysis, Google Sheets columns, and Slack alert message to match your organization’s threat triage process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "39689576-6034-497f-b0b7-0b45e7ec6ead",
